questions.modelAnswer:
int value;
do {
    printf("Enter 1-5: ");
    if (scanf("%d", &value) != 1)
        return 1;   /* not a number: give up */
} while (value < 1 || value > 5);
A do-while tests its condition after the body, so the prompt and read always happen once before the value is checked. With a while loop you would have to read once before the loop or give value an artificial starting value.

